  "authorNotes": "Built from the published Sylhet syllabus (lessons 15-22 and 24-29, lesson 23 excluded). Mohammadpur Final 2026 Class 3 Bangla was the main guide. Several of its questions were left out because they are outside the Sylhet scope: খরস্রোতা, ঘড়িয়াল, লুসাই পাহাড়, river pollution (lesson 14, নদীর দেশ), প্রতিপালন, and the items on আবু উমাইর's bird, learning ঈমান before the Quran, and the Prophet's kindness to children (none of these are in the textbook lessons in scope). Rows with no MP 2026 question of the same type were filled from MP Final 2025 / Half-yearly 2026 first and then from the book: synonyms (row 6, mostly NEW from lesson 19 exercise 7), sentence types (row 9, mostly NEW; the book never names the types, so I used the names MP uses: বর্ণনামূলক/নির্দেশমূলক, প্রশ্নবোধক, আদেশসূচক, অনুরোধসূচক, বিস্ময়সূচক — please confirm these are the names taught in class), poem extract (row 13, NEW, আদর্শ ছেলে), and the form (row 14, NEW from lesson 29; I chose the ফরম option, not তথ্যছক, per the either/or rule, and gave a short made-up scenario so the answers can be checked — switch to 'fill in your own details' if the teachers prefer). Row 8 (punctuation, 5 x 1) is one paragraph: the 5 items are the 5 marking points, so only the paragraph (stimulus) should be printed for the child. Row 15 has exactly one topic because the row has no choice; I used topic (খ) from MP 2025 instead of MP 2026's 'আবু বকর (রা)' because Abu Bakr is already the compulsory essay in row 12 — swap if you prefer, or add a choice. Two MP MCQs had a second defensible answer (মানবিক / উদাসীন) and were fixed. Duration '৩ ঘণ্টা' is copied from the brief's example; Mohammadpur's paper says ২ ঘণ্টা ৩০ মিনিট — please confirm. The MP Half-yearly 2025 'Class Three Bangla' file is actually a Class 1 class test, so it was not used."
